<title>LITHUANIA: GVT WILL TAKE $10 MILLION CREDIT TO BUY SOYA.</title>
<headline>GVT WILL TAKE $10 MILLION CREDIT TO BUY SOYA.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lithuanian government said on Monday that it will take a $10 million credit from the government of the United States to buy soya albumen additive for cattle feed.</p>
<p>&quot;The government decided to take up to $10 million in credits from the government of the United States to buy soya albumen additive to cattle grain in 1997 according to the programme PL-480,&quot; the government press office said in a statement.</p>
<p>The $10 million credit has a 20 year maturity with a three percent annual interest rate for the first five years and four percent interest rate for the rest of the period.</p>
<p>Approximately 33,000 tonnes of soya album additive might be bought for the credit while the country needs 48,000 tonnes, the government said.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
